  <h1>Quadrotor flight software</h1>
  <p class="meta">Personal project, ongoing since summer 2026 &middot; C++, Teensy 4.1, MATLAB, Unity tests &middot; <a href="https://github.com/jpyces/Active-Flight-Control">repo</a></p>

  <p>This is a complete guidance, navigation and control stack for a 7-inch quadrotor, with no flight-control libraries. I design each algorithm in MATLAB, port it to C++, and check it again with unit tests that run on a laptop. That catches most bugs before they get near hardware.</p>
  <p>It hasn't flown yet. Estimation, control and the flight state machine are ported and tested, and all four sensors run on the bench. Still to do before a first hover: flight-core integration, closed-loop simulation, the ESC driver and logging.</p>

