  <h2>A bug that only existed on the board</h2>
  <p>The sensor health checks passed every host-side test and then raised false alarms on real hardware. There were three causes stacked together.</p>
  <p>First, the GNSS reports at 10 Hz and the loop runs much faster, so most ticks have no new message, and the health logic read that as the sensor going quiet. Second, a receiver still acquiring its first fix is working correctly, but I was counting it as failing. It now gets a one-time grace window, and "has a fix" is reported separately from "is healthy". Third, the receiver library could consume its own "new data" flag when I read it, so freshness was unreliable. I now take freshness from the message's GNSS time-of-week advancing, which reading can't consume.</p>
  <p>Every driver now reports health and freshness separately, and the estimator only fuses a sample that is both.</p>
